# The main menus (docs/plans/realm-ui.md, Phase 1): the home menu, the campaign picker and the
# Load / Save dialog in the three realms. The profile (profile.set) picks the realm and fills the
# campaign row: none reached, campaign II reached, all three; Campaign resumes the campaign at its
# next mission, or opens the picker when more than one can be played, whose Continue starts the
# campaign picked; Continue loads the last save. Load / Save saves two games, reads their rows and
# preview, asks before overwriting, deletes one through its popup and loads the other. Each screen
# is checked for layout issues and saved as a screenshot under out/ui_menus/ (the CI artifact).
#
# The campaign's missions load the sample saves, so extract them first (unzip saves/sample_saves.zip,
# as CI does). The saves it writes (ui_menus, ui_menus_a and ui_menus_b, with their thumbnails) are
# deleted at the end. Run it with --fresh-profile, as CI does, so it starts from an empty profile
# and leaves the local one alone:
#   cargo run -p HeritageBuilder -- --fresh-profile --script crates/game/tests/scenarios/ui_menus.jsonl
{"method": "time.fixed_dt", "params": {"dt": 0.016667}}
{"method": "assert.eq", "params": {"query": "session.state", "path": "/menus_mode", "value": "Home"}}
{"method": "input.move", "params": {"park": true}}
{"method": "wait.frames", "params": {"frames": 3}}

